.TH CONVERT-CURRENCY 1
.SH NAME
convert-currency \- convert amounts using USD-based exchange rates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B convert-currency
.RB [ -h ]
.RB [ -s ]
.RI [ amount ]
.RI [ source " target ..."]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert an amount from the first currency to each target currency.
Currency codes are case-insensitive. Results are displayed to four decimal places.
Command-line values override configuration; missing values are prompted for.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Display command-line help.
.TP
.B -s, --show
Fetch and list available currencies without prompting for conversion inputs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B config.yaml
Optional YAML defaults in the current working directory. Supported keys are
url, amount, base_currency, and converting_currencies (a list).
The default URL is https://www.floatrates.com/daily/usd.json.
Custom feeds must use the same USD-based rate format.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B convert-currency 100 usd eur gbp
Convert 100 US dollars to euros and pounds.
.TP
.B python -m convert_currency --show
List available currencies using the installed Python package.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 for input, configuration, network, rate data, or unknown-currency
errors, and 2 for command-line syntax errors.
